{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451033-apocalypse-style-skin-dancers-for-forsaken","id":451033,"title":"Apocalypse style skin dancers for forsaken?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-20T17:01:59-07:00","id":451033,"title":"Apocalypse style skin dancers for forsaken?","content":"Anybody know of anything similar to this? Or does the universe of werewolf and its wolf blooded negate the need of such a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:05:13-07:00","id":451057,"title":"","content":"What's an Apocalypse style skin dancer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:16:08-07:00","id":451090,"title":"","content":"A kinfolk is pissed at their lot in life, learns a blasphemous ritual, skins 5 werewolves under the same moon (not necessarily the same month), performs said rite and becomes a werewolf with a major bone to pick. Also shunned by the spirit world and other werewolves for basically commiting high treason against their kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:38:23-07:00","id":451104,"title":"","content":"I could see that as a rite. I don't know if the spirits would shun them, either, I could see spirits finding them easier to influence because they don't have Luna's mandate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:43:54-07:00","id":451110,"title":"","content":"What like home grown bale hounds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:46:52-07:00","id":451112,"title":"","content":"That's not really what Bale Hounds are about. But depending on how heroic you want to make them, what I'm seeing is someone who gets the mechanical benefits of the forms,, able to change into all of them, though maybe not with each special blessing, like Badass Motherfucker. And they can transform and take advantage of Uratha's healing with them, but they don't really get the spirit benefits as they lack a werewolf's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:48:35-07:00","id":451113,"title":"","content":"Skin-dancers in WtA are Kinfolk that learn a rite that allows them to turn into full werewolves (though it involves killing and skinning five werewolves to make your new skin out of and is empowered by nasty spirits that taint you for it).<br /> <br /> I'm not aware of WtF retreading this sort of thing. The new Wolf-Blooded 2e rules seem to make this less important. Wolf-Blooded tells make them, by default, more &quot;special&quot; compared to WtA Kinfolk. As well there's less idea that you're either Uratha or Wolf-Blooded. Wolf-Blooded can change into Uratha; where Kinfolk were stuck always being kin.<br /> <br /> Though there doesn't seem to be anything stopping you from exploring it. There are nWOD rules for this that are detached from WtF in the book WOD: Skinchangers. If you want to have a Wolf-Blooded go that route, you could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:48:42-07:00","id":451114,"title":"","content":"I could see that. A pretender still just wolf blooded with a bit more power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:15:16-07:00","id":451126,"title":"","content":"Well, the section on Wolf Blooded pretty specifically states that there's no known way to predict or intentionally cause a First Change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: the Forsaken Second Edition, pg. 297</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as anyone knows, the First Change cannot be triggered. Even the most talented crescent-moons cannot chart or estimate the possibility of the Change occurring.</div> </div> </div> </div>So strictly speaking, I would say no, however...<br /> <br /> Later in that same paragraph it does say that some Lunes <i>claim</i> there is a rite that could allow a Wolf Blooded to become full werewolves, but that everyone who has ever tried it met with a horrible fate. I think the implication is supposed to be that either the Lunes are lying about the rite, or that it is incredibly difficult to perform correctly and disastrous if done wrong. However, if you really wanted to introduce Skin Thieves into Forsaken, this <i>could</i> be interpreted as a hint about the ritual you mentioned being a thing in Forsaken, and the reason those who have attempted it in the past all died is because they were killed by the werewolves they tried to skin (or by their packmates).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T20:23:57-07:00","id":451242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451033-apocalypse-style-skin-dancers-for-forsaken?p=451113#post451113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As well there's less idea that you're either Uratha or Wolf-Blooded. Wolf-Blooded can change into Uratha; where Kinfolk were stuck always being kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having only exposure to the corebook of WtA; would you elaborate on this part, please? I always thought Wolf-Blooded were the Kinfolk 2.0, so to speak. If Kinfolk couldn't become werewolves, then what (or who) could?<br /> <br /> Going back on the topic: <br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything stated directly in the 2ed Core that goes with what you want, but you could easily take the Skinner's Tell and twist it: allowing the skins worn to be Uratha as well and conferring all the perks/side-effects of the werewolf but lasting for a limited amount of time. Maybe a spirit teaches a Wolf-Blooded, or they discover on their own, an ability to force that particular Tell for that Particular ability. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T20:48:26-07:00","id":451261,"title":"","content":"Oh dude that it brilliant. Exactly this. And garou in apocalypse were born that way, you don't just upgrade. You're basically a chosen of the planet. Kinfolk are sub human breeding stock by comparison, according to the fianna at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T01:04:35-07:00","id":451365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451033-apocalypse-style-skin-dancers-for-forsaken?p=451242#post451242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having only exposure to the corebook of WtA; would you elaborate on this part, please? I always thought Wolf-Blooded were the Kinfolk 2.0, so to speak. If Kinfolk couldn't become werewolves, then what (or who) could?</div> </div> </div> </div>In WtA, the Garou and Kinfolk are born that way. While the books allow for some in-character ambiguity that could lead to a character thinking they were kin and then having a First Change by surprise, or thinking they were born to be a Garou and it never happening, such things are effectively decided at birth. The only way to become a Garou in WtA is to:<br /> <br /> 1) Be a Metis, born of two werewolves, which is an automatic werewolf birth (which has a lot of bad baggage for you to deal with).<br /> 2) Have one Werewolf parent, this has low odds; though increased odds if the other parent is kin and even more with Purebreed.<br /> 3) Have one Kinfolk parent, which has even worse odds; though again increased if the other parent is also kin, with Purebreed only mattering if both are Kin.<br /> <br /> WtF departed from this explicitly familial structure. Anyone could potentially be an Uratha or a Wolf-Blooded (even more in 2e now that Lunacy can spread Wolf-Blooded status). WtF 2e took it farther by removing the restrictions on werewolf-werewolf mating, and having the role of Wolf-Blooded be less breeding stock and more trusted friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T00:03:41-07:00","id":452330,"title":"","content":"One could do a skindancer using the shapeshifter rules from War against the pure, it specifically mentions that such shapeshifters could arise from genetics, or ritual, or curse, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> They wouldn't be quite as powerful as the uratha, though, but could be used if one wants do it yourself werewolves without one stealing the blessings of luna to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T02:22:18-07:00","id":452425,"title":"","content":"I think the Skinchangers rules in the, well, Skinchangers book, fit a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T02:32:14-07:00","id":452434,"title":"","content":"I was wondering how this thread got this far without mentioning the book that's all about dudes who skin animals and wear their skins to become creepy shapeshifting witches.<br /> <br /> Being that I don't actually know all that much about the content of Skinchangers, I'll note that Forsaken doesn't place the kind of emphasis Apocalypse did on codependence between the Uratha and Wolf-Blooded; there's not really a sense of a population crisis to drive the werewolves to dehumanize their relatives as mere breeding stock, and the second edition core consciously tries to avoid treating the Wolf-Blooded as a breeding herd. That said, if what you liked about the Skin Dancers was the sense of resentful and jealous former allies getting their own in awful ways, there's still plenty of room for a split between a pack's Uratha and their supporting human packmates. Alternatively, you might find a different kind of horror in the idea that Skinchangers might simply come out of nowhere, ambitious and mystically insightful humans emerging from the crowds to harry the pack seemingly at random, simply for their own benefit and puissance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T04:43:07-07:00","id":452516,"title":"","content":"Hey, just because it's not the default for werewolves to be dismissive of human and wolfblooded packmates doesn't mean that it doesn't happen. Some people are just dicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T11:20:48-07:00","id":452914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451033-apocalypse-style-skin-dancers-for-forsaken?p=452434#post452434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering how this thread got this far without mentioning the book that's all about dudes who skin animals and wear their skins to become creepy shapeshifting witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the book is about a lot more than that. While it does have people who wear the skins of animals, it's sort of like Immortals in that it offers you a way to build your own 'how do they do it' changer, so you could have the No Talisman aspect instead of having to skin anyone you just have a connection to a certain animal. One of the sample characters isn't even a human, Scavenger Wolf was a wolf spirit that wanted to do what werewolves did, though he does use skins. Another is a man who is able to turn into a swarm of ants by letting them bite him.<br /> <br /> The second chapter goes into specific and unique kinds of Claimed, including subcultures that do it as a tradition. The last chapter is one of my favorites, because it just has a bunch of oddities, like a rat with human intelligence, rules for chimera, and a class of lizard shapeshifters who are transformed through a virus. It's all followed up with suggestions on how to color your new shapeshifters based on the animals or insects chosen.<br /> <br /> Sorry to go on about it, but you said you don't know much about it and I just wanted to assure you it's about a lot more than people who skin animals for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:53:48-07:00","id":453133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/451033-apocalypse-style-skin-dancers-for-forsaken?p=452914#post452914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to go on about it, but you said you don't know much about it and I just wanted to assure you it's about a lot more than people who skin animals for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all; I appreciate it. I did recall that Skinchangers was broader than just skinner-witches, but it's always cool to hear the niche ideas and the versatility of a book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}